<h1>🏆 Game Mode Per App</h1>
<p class="meta">HTG Game Turbo · Feature Guide</p>

<div class="section">
<div class="highlight"><strong>What this does:</strong> Uses Android's official GameManager API (introduced in Android 12) to set a specific app to "Performance" mode — telling the system to prioritise CPU and GPU resources for that app to reduce throttling and improve FPS during gaming sessions.</div>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>How Android's Game Mode API Works</h2>
<p>Android 12 introduced <strong>GameManager</strong> — a system service that lets apps and system tools declare a "game mode" for specific packages. The three modes are:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Standard</strong> — default behavior, no changes</li>
<li><strong>Performance</strong> — system prioritises CPU/GPU for this app, may increase power consumption</li>
<li><strong>Battery</strong> — system reduces CPU/GPU to save battery for this app</li>
</ul>
<p>HTG Game Turbo sets the chosen app to <strong>Performance</strong> mode using Shizuku to run the following commands:</p>
<ul>
<li>Android 13+: <code>cmd game set --mode performance &lt;package&gt;</code></li>
<li>Android 12: <code>cmd game mode performance &lt;package&gt;</code></li>
</ul>
<p>Both commands are attempted automatically — whichever your Android version supports will be used.</p>

<div class="warning"><strong>Important limitation:</strong> Game Mode only works if the app being set has declared itself as a game in its manifest, OR if the OEM has implemented the full GameManager service. Many OEMs partially implement the API — the command accepts without error but has no actual effect on performance.</div>
</div>

<div class="section">
<h2>What "Verified" and "Not Verified" Mean in the App</h2>
<p>When you open Game Mode Per App, the app runs a quick test — it attempts to set a system package to Performance mode and reads the result back. Based on this:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>✅ Game Mode verified working</strong> — the system accepted the mode change and confirmed it. Your device's GameManager is active and responding.</li>
<li><strong>⚠️ Game Mode API is not responding</strong> — the verification test did not get a confirmed response. This does NOT always mean it won't work — it means verification couldn't confirm it. See below for your specific device.</li>
</ul>
</div>

